    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The envelope is designed to protect letters. It is so common today that we often "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "take",
            "ref": "v-take-for-granted"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " it "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "for granted",
            "ref": "v-take-for-granted"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". But did you know when and where the envelope first appeared? The history of envelopes is probably much longer than you think."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "It is believed the envelope first appeared in ancient China. It was used to protect "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "royal",
            "ref": "v-royal"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " messages. However, the early envelope was nothing like what we use today. It was made from "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "clay",
            "zh": "黏土"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and looked like a ball. After the message was placed inside, the envelope would be "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "sealed",
            "ref": "v-seal"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " with more clay. To read the message, one had to break the “envelope”."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The first paper envelope appeared around 200 BCE. It was also invented by the Chinese. However, at first, people used it only to send money as gifts to each other. It was not until around the seventh century that it was used for sending messages. The design of the early paper envelope was very simple. It was just a sheet of paper "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "folded",
            "ref": "v-fold"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and sealed with "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "wax",
            "zh": "蜡"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Since the envelope was made completely by hand, it was very expensive."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "In the 19th century, printing and "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "manufacturing",
            "ref": "v-manufacturing"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " methods improved greatly. In 1853, American inventor Russel Hawes invented an envelope maker. The machine could produce about 12,500 envelopes every day. With these improvements, the cost of envelopes went down. The design also became more complex."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Today, emails have become more popular than handwritten letters. However, billions of envelopes are used worldwide every year. They are still part of modern life."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      }
    ]
  },
